  "qa": {
    "status": "pass",
    "method": "layout_build: vertex-grid painting and hygiene, corner-Wang tile lookup, seeded scatter; collision.rects re-rasterised on the 4 px raster of the blocking set; reachability with the vendored forge_nav (D4) on the bundle's full blocking set (D2: collision.solids and rects, object footprints, the placed tiles' collision), read back as every consumer reads it: footprint validity (r=7, ySquash=0.9) at 4 px grid nodes, 4-neighbour moves with segmentClear and the thin-gap rule, BFS from the first spawn, N14 targets",
    "notProven": [
      "How the map looks: open preview.png and debug.png (magenta = walkable but unreachable, dark = too tight for the actor).",
      "collision.rects are the 4 px cells whose centre the exact blockers cover; an engine that collides with the rects alone gets that cell approximation of prop footprints (the proof covers the rects together with the exact shapes).",
      "Reachability is proven for one actor size; larger actors, jumping, doors that open and moving objects are not simulated.",
      "Tile seams: layout_build trusts the tileset manifest's seam proof."
